        "narration": "Here's the whole experience, right in the FinS solution. It starts with the lender's credit policy — you upload the source documents, and an agent reads them and generates the data-validation rules: over two hundred, across twenty-one sources. Then you review. The rules appear as a decision-model tree, right beside the source document — rule groups and conditions, all editable. Confirm what's correct, reorder, or refine any rule, with the policy always in view. Editing is direct: name a rule, set its group, adjust its fields, and save — no code. Then the documents are classified and validated against the model, so the taxonomy is scored and reviewed. And finally, publish — rules, models, and taxonomy all signed off, the configuration stamped with its decision model."
      },
      "transitionOverlap": 0.0
    },
